// ---- landscaping brushes (terrain, strata, boulders, water, trees, paths, bridges) — see references/landscaping.md --
export * from "./terrain.mjs";

// ---- roofs by style name (gable, hip, pyramid, mansard, gambrel, flat-parapet, shed, dutch-gable) — references/roofs.md
export * from "./roofs.mjs";

// ---- facade brushes (signage, pilasters, surrounds, glazing, fixtures, planters) — references/detail-language.md -----
// Each is a function on a grid (writes only where it may: air for projections, plain wall for in-place trim; returns
- [ ] P1 shell  - [ ] P2 front  - [ ] P3 roofs  - [ ] P4 openings  - [ ] P5 ornament  - [ ] P6 site

## NOTES for workers
- Never write into a reserved cell or into air a prior part left (runParts refuses). P1 leaves: openings, porch mouth, column cells, pilaster/cornice/bracket cells, stair holes, skylight.
- Plan coordinates only; the cheek wins at (10,1,2),(14,1,2) over the fence. Mind the +1 proud cells: z=3 on the bay, z=6 main wall.
- Front is NORTH. Stairs `facing` = side of the high back. Cornice lips: half=top, facing=south.
- Render the north elevation after each part and look; keep the roof flat, nothing above y=20 except the chimney pots (y21).
